       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is 5 times the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day (the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day). A single 4,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. A dose like this risks GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and metabolic toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you really do want 4000 mg per dose, tell me and add a note with the rationale, and I'll enter it. Otherwise, tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
