      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. That is far above the maximum daily dose and is in the range where serious toxicity is expected: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. For a 70 kg patient, a single 4,000 mg dose is about 57 mg/kg, which is already above the level at which toxicity is seen in overdose. I know of no indication that calls for this dose, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily\n- 800 mg PO three times daily\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you're aiming for stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a different regimen. Examples are scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or another agent you choose. If you believe this dose is intended, please contact pharmacy directly. They can review it with you and put it through whatever override process your hospital requires."
      }
